* [ Career ][84] * [ Starting work at Jenoptik ][85] * [ Jenoptik as an employer ][86] * [ Partners ][87] * [ Job offers ][88] * [ Events ][89] * Search search [ Close ][90] New CEO for Jenoptik Dr. Dominic Dorfner was appointed to become the new CEO of JENOPTIK AG. He will assume the position in August 2026. * [ ## Significant increase in orders and earningsHalf-year results * Strong order intake momentum, particularly in OEM businesses * Revenue slightly above prior year; profitability significantly improved * Guidance for 2026 specified learn more ][91] * [ ## Advanced solutions for life sciences and medical technology Mastering challenges in diagnostics and therapy for a better future. more ][92] * [ ## Optical systems for semiconductor equipment From individual modules to complete systems – we're your experienced partner for advanced, high-quality semiconductor equipment manufacturing. discover more ][93] * [ ## High-tech fab in Dresden, Germany Manufacturing micro-optics for the semiconductor equipment industry discover more ][94] * [ ## Safe actions save lives Driver inattention and speeding are major causes of crashes in work zones. Discover our traffic law enforcement solutions that help keep work zones safe for all road users. explore ][95] Prev Next # About Jenoptik We are a global technology group operating in the photonics market. Our growth areas include semiconductors, medical technology, metrology, and smart mobility. Almost 4,500 employees work worldwide in the Jenoptik Group, which is headquartered in Jena (Germany). JENOPTIK AG is listed on the German Stock Exchange in Frankfurt. [ Read more ][96] ## Locations worldwide [][97] [ Our locations ][98] ## News [ 12 August 2026 ### Jenoptik reports significant increase in orders and earnings in the first half of 2026 Strong order intake momentum, particularly in the OEM businesses. Revenue slightly above prior year; profitability significantly improved. Guidance for 2026 specified. read more ][99] [ [Jenoptik-Vorstand ab August 2026] 03 August 2026 ### Dr. Dominic Dorfner assumes office as CEO of JENOPTIK AG The Supervisory Board approves reorganization of Executive Board responsibilities and creates new CTO/COO role. read more ][100] [ [Brian Soller] 11 June 2026 ### Brian Soller named President of JENOPTIK Optical Systems, LLC He will be responsible for the efficient operation, strategic development and sustainable growth of Jenoptik’s U.S. optics and photonics business. read more ][101] [ [Flags More Light] 10 June 2026 ### Daniela Mattheus re-elected as Chair of the Supervisory Board of JENOPTIK AG At its meeting on June 9, 2026, held following the Annual General Meeting, the Supervisory Board of JENOPTIK AG, Jena, unanimously re-elected Daniela Mattheus as Chair of the Supervisory Board. read more ][102] ## Enabling the Amazing [Video] ## Blog [ **A true asset in PIC testing** How to test electrical and optical functions on chips efficiently and simultaneously ][103] [ [Car with lights] **The power of light in car design** Learn how our laser machines contribute to individual patterns and designs for more safety, brand visualization and well-being in the automotive future. ][104] [ [Mars Mission Rover] **Cutting edge lens assemblies for Mars mission** A journey into space requires unique demands. Discover what our engineers developed for the Mars 2020 mission! ][105] [ [fluorescence] **Competitive advantage in digital cell imaging** Here’s how to successfully cater to the market of life science and in vitro diagnostics. ][106] [To the Blog][107] ## Enabling brighter futures with the power of light – and excellent career opportunities for you We set ourselves the highest technological standards, working in dynamic teams and providing excellent and innovative products. Whether it be for training, employment, job placement or for a dissertation: You’ll find the right job with us. [ To the Job Offers ][108] [Career at Jenoptik] ## 4,500 employees worldwide [ [Pr