SML\n    * Back\n    * [About ASML overview][5]\n    * [Vision & mission][6]\n    * [Organization][7]\n    * [History][8]\n    * [Locations][9]\n  * [Stories][10]\n  * Governance\n    * Back\n    * [Governance overview][11]\n    * [Board of Management][12]\n    * [Supervisory Board][13]\n    * [Shareholders][14]\n    * [Code of Conduct][15]\n    * [How we manage risk][16]\n    * [Auditors][17]\n    * [Governance downloads][18]\n  * [Sustainability][19]\n  * Community engagement\n    * Back\n    * [Community engagement overview][20]\n    * [Education][21]\n    * [Culture][22]\n    * [Local outreach][23]\n* Careers\n  * Back\n  * [Careers overview][24]\n  * [Search jobs][25]\n  * [Interviewing at ASML][26]\n  * Working at ASML\n    * Back\n    * [Working at ASML overview][27]\n    * [The Netherlands][28]\n    * [United States][29]\n    * [Taiwan][30]\n    * [South Korea][31]\n    * [China][32]\n    * [Japan][33]\n    * [Germany][34]\n  * [Technical fields][35]\n  * [Teams][36]\n  * Students & graduates\n    * Back\n    * [Students & graduates overview][37]\n    * [Early careers][38]\n    * [The Netherlands][39]\n    * [United States][40]\n    * [Taiwan][41]\n    * [South Korea][42]\n    * [China][43]\n* Technology\n  * Back\n  * [Technology overview][44]\n  * All about chips\n    * Back\n    * [All about chips overview][45]\n    * [The basics][46]\n    * [How microchips are made][47]\n    * [Moore's Law][48]\n  * Lithography principles\n    * Back\n    * [Lithography principles overview][49]\n    * [The Rayleigh criterion][50]\n    * [Light & lasers][51]\n    * [Lenses & mirrors][52]\n    * [Mechanics & mechatronics][53]\n    * [Measuring accuracy][54]\n    * [Pushing k1 further][55]\n  * How we innovate\n    * Back\n    * [How we innovate overview][56]\n    * [Fellows][57]\n  * [Software][58]\n* Products\n  * Back\n  * [Products overview][59]\n  * [EUV lithography][60]\n  * [DUV lithography][61]\n  * [Refurbished systems][62]\n  * [Metrology & inspection][63]\n  * [Computational lithography][64]\n  * [Customer support][65]\n* News\n  * Back\n  * [News overview][66]\n  * [Press releases & announcements][67]\n  * [Share buyback][68]\n  * [Media library][69]\n  * [Contact Media Relations][70]\n  * [News alerts][71]\n* Investors\n  * Back\n  * [Investors overview][72]\n  * Why invest in ASML\n    * Back\n    * [Why invest in ASML overview][73]\n    * [Fact Sheet][74]\n    * [Financial strategy][75]\n    * [Capital return & financing][76]\n    * [Share buyback][77]\n  * [Annual reports][78]\n  * Financial results\n    * Back\n    * [Financial results overview][79]\n    * [Q2 2026][80]\n    * [Q1 2026][81]\n    * [Q4 2025][82]\n    * [Q3 2025][83]\n    * [Q2 2025][84]\n    * [Q1 2025][85]\n  * [Financial overview][86]\n  * Shares\n    * Back\n    * [Shares overview][87]\n    * [Share price][88]\n    * [SEC filings][89]\n    * [Analyst coverage][90]\n  * [Investor days][91]\n  * [Financial calendar][92]\n  * [Contact Investor Relations][93]\n* [Contact us][94]\n* [SupplierNet][95]\n* [CustomerNet][96]\n\n## Search\n\nSearch\n[ASML TV Image 1920 x 958-ASML_High_NA_Still_OI_F0_01]\n\n# Changing the world, one nanometer at a time\n\nASML enables the world’s leading chipmakers to produce the microchips that power today’s world.\n\n### Quick Links\n* [\n  \n  About ASML\n  \n  ][97]\n* [\n  \n  Careers\n  \n  ][98]\n* [\n  \n  Products\n  \n  ][99]\n* [\n  \n  Financial results\n  \n  ][100]\n\nWe're powering technology forward\n\nIn fact, we’re probably a part of the electronic device you’re using right now. Our lithography\ntechnology is fundamental to mass producing semiconductor chips. With it, the world’s top chipmakers\nare creating microchips that are more powerful, faster and energy efficient.\n\n\n[See all products][101]\n\nStory - June 12, 2026\n\nThe machines behind the machines\nHow ASML is applying AI-native engineering for the next technology era \n[Read more][102]\nAt a glance\n\nWho we are, what we do and why it matters\n\n[About ASML][103]\nLatest press releas"}}, "page_text": "[Skip to main content][1] [[ASML Logo]][2] [ Saved jobs ][3] We saved your job * Company * Back * [Company overview][4] * About ASML * Back * [About ASML overview][5] * [Vision & mission][6] * [Organization][7] * [History][8] * [Locations][9] * [Stories][10] * Governance * Back * [Governance overview][11] * [Board of Management][12] * [Supervisory Board][13] * [Shareholders][14] * [Code of Conduct][15] * [How we manage risk][16] * [Auditors][17] * [Governance downloads][18] * [Sustainability][19] * Community engagement * Back * [Community engagement overview][20] * [Education][21] * [Culture][22] * [Local outreach][23] * Careers * Back * [Careers overview][24] * [Search jobs][25] * [Interviewing at ASML][26] * Working at ASML * Back * [Working at ASML overview][27] * [The Netherlands][28] * [United States][29] * [Taiwan][30] * [South Korea][31] * [China][32] * [Japan][33] * [Germany][34] * [Technical fields][35] * [Teams][36] * Students & graduates * Back * [Students & graduates overview][37] * [Early careers][38] * [The Netherlands][39] * [United States][40] * [Taiwan][41] * [South Korea][42] * [China][43] * Technology * Back * [Technology overview][44] * All about chips * Back * [All about chips overview][45] * [The basics][46] * [How microchips are made][47] * [Moore's Law][48] * Lithography principles * Back * [Lithography principles overview][49] * [The Rayleigh criterion][50] * [Light & lasers][51] * [Lenses & mirrors][52] * [Mechanics & mechatronics][53] * [Measuring accuracy][54] * [Pushing k1 further][55] * How we innovate * Back * [How we innovate overview][56] * [Fellows][57] * [Software][58] * Products * Back * [Products overview][59] * [EUV lithography][60] * [DUV lithography][61] * [Refurbished systems][62] * [Metrology & inspection][63] * [Computational lithography][64] * [Customer support][65] * News * Back * [News overview][66] * [Press releases & announcements][67] * [Share buyback][68] * [Media library][69] * [Contact Media Relations][70] * [News alerts][71] * Investors * Back * [Investors overview][72] * Why invest in ASML * Back * [Why invest in ASML overview][73] * [Fact Sheet][74] * [Financial strategy][75] * [Capital return & financing][76] * [Share buyback][77] * [Annual reports][78] * Financial results * Back * [Financial results overview][79] * [Q2 2026][80] * [Q1 2026][81] * [Q4 2025][82] * [Q3 2025][83] * [Q2 2025][84] * [Q1 2025][85] * [Financial overview][86] * Shares * Back * [Shares overview][87] * [Share price][88] * [SEC filings][89] * [Analyst coverage][90] * [Investor days][91] * [Financial calendar][92] * [Contact Investor Relations][93] * [Contact us][94] * [SupplierNet][95] * [CustomerNet][96] ## Search Search [ASML TV Image 1920 x 958-ASML_High_NA_Still_OI_F0_01] # Changing the world, one nanometer at a time ASML enables the world’s leading chipmakers to produce the microchips that power today’s world. ### Quick Links * [ About ASML ][97] * [ Careers ][98] * [ Products ][99] * [ Financial results ][100] We're powering technology forward In fact, we’re probably a part of the electronic device you’re using right now. Our lithography technology is fundamental to mass producing semiconductor chips. With it, the world’s top chipmakers are creating microchips that are more powerful, faster and energy efficient. [See all products][101] Story - June 12, 2026 The machines behind the machines How ASML is applying AI-native engineering for the next technology era [Read more][102] At a glance Who we are, what we do and why it matters [About ASML][103] Latest press releases * [ July 15, 2026 High NA EUV reaches new readiness milestone with first high-volume Logic product ][104] * [ July 15, 2026 ASML reports €9.3 billion total net sales and €2.9 billion net income in Q2 2026 ][105] * [ May 16, 2026 Tata Electronics and ASML Announce Strategic Partnership to Advance the Semiconductor Manufacturing Ecosystem in India ][106] [ASML TV Image 1920 x 958-ASML_High_NA_4K_Clean_H264_00_54_2] Our technology Using light to drive microchip innovation [About lithography][107] ## Discover holistic lithography At ASML, our unique approach supports chipmakers in optimizing the chip patterning process at every stage from R&D to volume manufacturing. ## Enable third party cookies to play this video DisabledEnabled Our global presence ## Three continents, over 60 locations * [ ### The Netherlands Read more ASML is headquartered in Veldhoven amid a thriving ecosystem of high-tech companies. Our headquarters is home to more than half of all our employees. ][108] * [ ### United States Read more With 14 customer support sites, two factories, and three R&D centers, our US locations service Intel and other customers and contribute to our holistic product portfolio. ][109] * [ [cleanroom euv wafer stage training Taiwan] ### Taiwan Read more We have the largest ASML manufacturing site in Asia as well as two training centers, play an essential role in the rapidly growing e-beam market, and work closely with TSMC and major semiconductor fabs. ][110] * [ [cleanroom euv wafer stage training Korea] ### South Korea Read more Our teams in South Korea work closely with Samsung and other customers and have five locations that include a global distribution center and 4 training centers. ][111] * [ ### Chinese mainland Read more We support both global big-name customers and fast-growing local customers with 12 customer support sites, two R&D centers, and one training center. ][112] * [ ### Germany Read more Our Germany locations, such as Berlin and Dresden, specialize in optical manufacturing technology, precision manufacturing, as well as software development and customer support. ][113] * [ [ASML cleanroom] ### Japan Read more Japan is home to tech giants and major semiconductor players, with whom ASML collaborates closely. You can help to advance technology – and your career. ][114] ### Explore career opportunities to help develop the technology behind the world’s most powerful ### microchips. [Work at ASML][115] [[Abstract close‑up of semiconductor chip patterns]][116] [ Our 2025 Annual Report ][117] [Explore the highlights][118] ## Learn * [History][119] * [Products][120] * [Technology][121] * [Sustainability][122] * [News][123] ## Work At ASML * [Job search][124] * [Careers][125] * [Organization][126] * [Locations][127] ## Invest * [Why invest in ASML][128] * [Annual report][129] * [Financial results][130] * [Investor days][131] * [Shares][132] ## Get in touch * [Contact information][133] * [Contact Media Relations][134] * [Contact Investor Relations][135] * [CustomerNet][136] * [SupplierNet][137] #### Social Media * [][138] * [][139] * [][140] * [][141] * [][142] * [][143] Manage cookie settings Copyright © 2019-2026 (ASML) All Rights Reserved [Terms of use][144] [Privacy][145] [Cookies][146] [Terms & conditions][147] [Accessibility][148] [1]: #content [2]: /en [3]: /en/careers/saved-jobs [4]: /en/company [5]: /en/company/about-asml [6]: /en/company/about-asml/vision-and-mission [7]: /en/company/about-asml/organization [8]: /en/company/about-asml/history [9]: /en/company/about-asml/locations [10]: /en/company/stories [11]: /en/company/governance [12]: /en/company/governance/board-of-management [13]: /en/company/governance/supervisory-board [14]: /en/company/governance/shareholders [15]: /en/company/governance/code-of-conduct [16]: /en/company/governance/risk [17]: /en/company/governance/auditors [18]: /en/company/governance/governance-downloads [19]: /en/company/sustainability [20]: /en/company/community-engagement [21]: /en/company/community-engagement/education [22]: /en/company/community-engagement/culture [23]: /en/company/community-engagement/local-outreach [24]: /en/careers [25]: /en/careers/find-your-job [26]: /en/careers/interview-tips [27]: /en/careers/working-at-asml [28]: /en/careers/working-at-asml/netherlands [29]: /en/careers/working-at-asml/united-states [30]: /en/careers/working-