lor LEDs", "UV-C LEDs", "IR LEDs", "Multi color LEDs", "LED modules", "LED accessories"]}, {"name": "Drivers", "category": "Lighting components", "features": ["LED drivers"]}, {"name": "Lasers", "category": "Light emitters", "features": ["Color lasers (EEL)", "Color lasers (VCSEL)", "IR lasers (EEL)", "IR lasers (VCSEL)"]}, {"name": "Photodetectors", "category": "Optical sensors", "features": ["Photodiodes", "Phototransistors"]}, {"name": "Multi chips", "category": "Optical components"}, {"name": "Optical modules", "category": "Optical components"}, {"name": "Sensor solutions", "category": "Sensor components", "features": ["Active noise cancellation", "Ambient light, color, spectral & proximity sensors", "Analog frontend", "CMOS image sensors", "Direct time-of-flight sensors (dToF)", "Optical force sensors"]}, {"name": "Interfaces", "category": "Integrated circuits", "features": ["Sensor interfaces"]}, {"name": "Lamps", "category": "Lighting products", "features": ["Automotive lamps"]}, {"name": "Boards, kits & accessories", "category": "Development tools"}, {"name": "OSRAM SYNIOS™ P2222", "category": "LED", "features": ["Standard LED for automotive signaling", "Small package outline", "Available in all application-specific colors"]}, {"name": "OSRAM FIREFLY™ SFH 4030B", "category": "Infrared emitter", "features": ["940 nm wavelength", "Thinfilm IR:6 chip technology", "High brightness infrared illumination", "Extended battery life", "Dark package for invisible integration"]}, {"name": "ams TMF8829", "category": "Time-of-flight sensor", "features": ["Direct ToF with configurable resolution (8x8, 16x16, 32x32, 48x32)", "SPAD, TDC, histogram technology", "Detection range up to 11000 mm", "80° field of view", "On-chip processing", "I3C/I2C/SPI interface", "0.25 mm resolution", "Compact 5.7 mm x 2.9 mm x 1.5 mm optical module"]}, {"name": "ams TMF8806", "category": "Time-of-flight sensor", "features": ["1D ToF sensor", "SPAD, TDC, histogram technology", "500 cm detection range (extendable to 1000 cm with firmware)", "Single modular package with VCSEL"]}, {"name": "ams AS1181", "category": "Driver IC", "features": ["8-channel LED and VCSEL driver"]}], "services": ["Full-Service Foundry", "Product support", "Design support", "Technical support", "Partner network"], "industries": ["Automotive & mobility", "Industrial", "Medical & health", "Mobile & wearables", "Lighting", "Computing"], "key_markets": []}, "financials": {"key_numbers": ["120 years of the OSRAM brand"], "employee_count": null, "scale_signals": ["global leader"]}, "relationships": {"customers": [], "investors": []}, "intel": "ams OSRAM is a global leader in innovative light and sensor solutions, offering a broad portfolio of LEDs, lasers, photodetectors, sensors, and optical components. The company serves multiple industries including automotive, industrial, medical, mobile/wearables, lighting, and computing. Recent news highlights a trademark licensing agreement with USHIO Industry & Entertainment for OSRAM-branded professional technical lighting products, and the company has published its 2025 Annual Report. With a 120-year brand heritage, ams OSRAM emphasizes innovation in areas like LiDAR, humanoid robotics, and microLED data transmitters.", "media": {"articles": [], "press_releases": [], "investor_presentations": []}}, "page_text": "", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "ams AG — channel participant (google_ai_overview). Verify: ams AG designs and manufactures sensor and analog chips, building technology for the semiconductor market. | Sensor and analog chips | Austria | Austria", "role_description": "Solution Provider"}}, "X Score": "64", "Y Score": "62", "Overall Score": "63", "Industry Category": "ICT, Automation, Semiconductor / Semiconductors", "Quadrant": "Trailblazers"}, {"Company": "GlobalFoundries (already listed)", "Website": "https://gf.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "United States", "Continent / Geography": "NA(United States)", "Operational Presence": "United States", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Already listed.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Solution Provider", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "US", "Region Code": "NA", "Summary": "GlobalFoundries (already listed) — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: GlobalFoundries is a semiconductor foundry, manufacturing chips.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Solution Provider", "verify_confidence": "95", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "gf.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "GlobalFoundries", "domain": "gf.com", "description": "A leading manufacturer of essential semiconductors, enabling AI at scale from the cloud to the physical world.", "headquarters": "Malta, New York, USA", "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null}, "business": {"products": [{"name": "Advanced packaging", "category": "Technology", "features": "2.5D/3D, W2W and D2W bonding, interposer-based architectures for heterogeneous integration; includes SLATE wafer-to-wafer bonding technology for 3D integration.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "CMOS", "category": "Technology", "features": "Includes FDX FD-SOI, Feature-rich CMOS, and FinFET; delivers power efficiency and performance with competitive PPA, leading RF and application-optimized features.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Power solutions", "category": "Technology", "features": "BCD and Power GaN solutions deliver high power density, efficiency and integrated reliability for scalable power architectures across consumer and industrial applications.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Quantum technology", "category": "Technology", "features": "Bridges quantum from research to deployable systems with scalable semiconductor technologies, advanced manufacturing and system-level integration.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "RF-SOI", "category": "Technology", "features": "High performance, signal power and reliability for mobile, automotive, infrastructure and aerospace and defense applications.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "SiGe", "category": "Technology", "features": "High performance, signal power and reliability for mobile, automotive, infrastructure and aerospace and defense applications.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "RF GaN", "category": "Technology", "features": "GaN-on-silicon approach combines performance advantages of GaN with cost advantages and volume of 200mm silicon manufacturing.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Silicon photonics", "category": "Technology", "features": "Energy-efficient optical connectivity for pluggables and co-packaged optics; scalable, production-proven platform for high-bandwidth optical interconnects.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "MIPS", "category": "Compute platform", "features": "A GlobalFoundries company delivering virtual platforms, standards-based compute and ASSP design capabilities for making software into silicon.", "pricing": null}], "services": [{"name": "Advanced packaging centers", "category": "Manufacturing service", "features": "Support for advanced packaging technologies and heterogeneous integration.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "GlobalShuttle™ MPW program", "category": "Manufacturing service", "features": "Multi-project wafer program for prototyping and low-volume production.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Quality & certifications", "category": "Quality service", "features": "Quality and certification services for semiconductor manufacturing.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Digital manufacturing", "category": "Manufacturing service", "features": "Digital manufacturing capabilities and services.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "GF Connect customer portal", "category": "Customer portal", "features": "Portal for customer access to manufacturing and design resources.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "MIPS Atlas portal", "category": "Customer portal", "features": "Portal for MIPS-related design and compute resources.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "GlobalSolutions™ ecosystem", "category": "Partner ecosystem", "features": "Ecosystem of partners and solutions for design and manufacturing.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Value-added partner program", "category": "Partner program", "features": "Program for value-added partners to collaborate with GF.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Process design kits (PDK)", "category": "Design support", "features": "PDKs for various GF technology platforms.", "pricing": null}, {"name": "Design support resources", "category": "Design support", "features": "Comprehensive design support including PDKs, in-house expertise and global partner networks.", "pricing": null}], "industries": ["Aerospace & defense", "Automotive", "Data center & communications infrastructure", "Home & industrial IoT", "Physical AI", "Smart mobile devices"], "key_markets": ["North America", "EMEA", "APAC", "United States", "Europe", "Asia", "Germany", "Singapore", "China"]}, "financials": {"key_numbers": ["$300 million LOI with U.S. Department of Commerce", "12th annual Sustainability Report", "200mm silicon manufacturing"], "employee_count": null}, "relationships": {"customers": [], "investors": []}, "intel": "GlobalFoundries is a leading semiconductor manufacturer with a differentiated specialty technology portfolio spanning RF, power, advanced packaging, silicon photonics, and quantum. The recent $300M LOI with the U.S. Department of Commerce underscores its strategic investment in silicon photonics for AI and high-performance computing data centers. Its global manufacturing footprint across the U.S., Europe, and Asia provides supply-chain resilience and customer proximity. Key watch items include the commercialization of SLATE advanced packaging for cellular front-ends and the ramp of RF GaN on 200mm silicon. Actionable opportunities: monitor GF's silicon photonics roadmap, assess its competitive position in automotive and industrial IoT markets, and track further government/CHIPS-related funding.", "location": {"headquarters": "Malta, New York, USA", "offices": ["Malta, New York", "Burlington, Vermont", "Dresden, Germany", "Singapore", "Guangzhou"], "countries": ["United States", "Germany", "Singapore", "China"], "regions_served": ["North America", "EMEA", "APAC"]}, "media": {"articles": [], "press_releases": [], "investor_presentations": []}}, "page_text": "", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "GlobalFoundries (already listed) — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: GlobalFoundries is a semiconductor foundry, manufacturing chips. | Already listed. | United States | United States", "role_description": "Solution Provider"}}, "X Score": "64", "Y Score": "62", "Overall Score": "63", "Industry Category": "ICT, Automation, Semiconductor / Semiconductors", "Quadrant": "Trailblazers"}, {"Company": "Semicab", "Website": "https://www.semicab.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "India", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(India)", "Operational Presence": "India", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Semicab is an Indian semiconductor company specializing in power management ICs and analog mixed-signal products.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Solution Provider", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Semicab — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Specializes in power management ICs and analog mixed-signal products, indicating design and manufacturing.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Solution Provider", "verify_confidence": "90", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "semicab.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "semicab.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "[\nSkip to main content\n][1]\n[\n][2]\nContact Sales\n[\n][3]\nContact Sales\n\n1 in 3 truck miles runs empty.\nEveryone pays for it.\n\nThis is not the cost of logistics. It is the cost of a broken design.\n\n# **SemiCab** changes the design.\n\nSo performance improves for every participant, by design, not by effort.\n\nTalk to an expert\n\nTechnology trusted across Fortune 500 and large enterprise networks\n\nTHE SYSTEM-LEVEL ANSWER\n\n## Everyone optimizes their part. No one optimizes the whole.\n\nSemiCab operates at the level where freight performance is shaped: across demand, capacity,\nlocations and participants.\n\nReach out to us\n\n### Orchestrate\n\nRoute, space, weight, time, sequence, and location are one problem.\n\n### Optimize\n\nMake decisions for the whole, not one load at a time.\n\n### Execute\n\nFlow optimized plans into existing ERP and TMS workflows.\n\n## One network.\n## Built to improve outcomes for every participant.\n\nSee SemiCab Apex\n\n### LSPs and 3PLs\n\nUnlock true 5PL advantage by optimizing across your entire customer network. Win with outcomes\ncompetitors cannot replicate.\n\nEnterprise Shippers\n\nReduce structural freight cost beyond rate negotiation. Turn transportation into a more controllable\nP&L lever.\n\nCarriers\n\nGet paid for more loaded miles. Gain more predictable utilization and earnings.\n\nTHE SEMICAB DIFFERENCE\n\n## Intelligence designed into the system\n\n### AI, by design\n\nOptimization, forecasting and specialized agents embedded inside the planning logic.\n\n### Ecosystem-led\n\nIndependent participants benefit from one orchestrated network without changing how they operate day\nto day.\n\n### Sustainable through efficiency\n\nFewer empty miles mean lower cost, lower fuel consumption and fewer emissions.\n\nReach out to us\n\nStructural improvement at scale\n\n## Better outcomes, by Design\n\nOutcomes measured across networks running on **SemiCab technology** in India.\n\n70%+\n\nReduction in empty miles\n\n7%\n\nReduction in FTL spend\n\n~40%\n\nImprovement in asset productivity\n\n5%\n\nSpot-load reliance (reduction from ~15%)\n\nAsian Paints LimitedMTRApollo Tyres\n01/03\n\n### We partnered with SemiCab early because we trusted their vision for network-level logistics.\n\nToday, they are one of our top transport partners in India, combining strong service performance\nwith a more sustainable, data-driven operating model.\n\nSanchit Sasidhara\n\nPlanning & Purchase, Asian Paints\n\n### SemiCab has been a reliable partner for our first-mile vehicle placement requirements over the\n### past six months.\n\nTheir timely vehicle placements and cooperative team have supported the smooth functioning of our\noperations. We appreciate their responsiveness and service commitment, and look forward to\ncontinuing our association.\n\nMTR\n\n### At Apollo Tyres, sustainability is a long-term commitment that extends across our entire value\n### chain, including logistics.\n\nOur partnership with SemiCab has helped us rethink how our transportation network is planned and\noperated, bringing greater efficiency, reliability, and structural improvement into the system. We\nsee SemiCab’s network-led approach as an important enabler in building a more responsible and\nfuture-ready supply chain.\n\nRajshekhara Reddy\n\nGroup head - Global Logistics, Apollo Tyres\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### How is Orchestrated Collaboration™ different from contractual freight arrangements?\n\nContracts coordinate predefined static commitments between a fixed set of parties. When demand,\ncapacity or operating conditions change, the arrangement often becomes ineffective or may need to be\nrenegotiated.\n\nOrchestrated Collaboration™ uses a neutral orchestration layer to continuously identify\nopportunities across the network dynamically, within each participant’s agreed commercial and\noperating constraints.\n\n### How does network-wide optimization account for each participant’s priorities?\n\nEach participant’s service levels, commercial rules and operating constraints remain part of the\nplan.\n\nSemiCab activates opportunities where networ"}}, "page_text": "[ Skip to main content ][1] [ ][2] Contact Sales [ ][3] Contact Sales 1 in 3 truck miles runs empty. Everyone pays for it. This is not the cost of logistics. It is the cost of a broken design. # **SemiCab** changes the design. So performance improves for every participant, by design, not by effort. Talk to an expert Technology trusted across Fortune 500 and large enterprise networks THE SYSTEM-LEVEL ANSWER ## Everyone optimizes their part. No one optimizes the whole. SemiCab operates at the level where freight performance is shaped: across demand, capacity, locations and participants. Reach out to us ### Orchestrate Route, space, weight, time, sequence, and location are one problem. ### Optimize Make decisions for the whole, not one load at a time. ### Execute Flow optimized plans into existing ERP and TMS workflows. ## One network. ## Built to improve outcomes for every participant. See SemiCab Apex ### LSPs and 3PLs Unlock true 5PL advantage by optimizing across your entire customer network. Win with outcomes competitors cannot replicate. Enterprise Shippers Reduce structural freight cost beyond rate negotiation. Turn transportation into a more controllable P&L lever. Carriers Get paid for more loaded miles. Gain more predictable utilization and earnings. THE SEMICAB DIFFERENCE ## Intelligence designed into the system ### AI, by design Optimization, forecasting and specialized agents embedded inside the planning logic. ### Ecosystem-led Independent participants benefit from one orchestrated network without changing how they operate day to day. ### Sustainable through efficiency Fewer empty miles mean lower cost, lower fuel consumption and fewer emissions. Reach out to us Structural improvement at scale ## Better outcomes, by Design Outcomes measured across networks running on **SemiCab technology** in India. 70%+ Reduction in empty miles 7% Reduction in FTL spend ~40% Improvement in asset productivity 5% Spot-load reliance (reduction from ~15%) Asian Paints LimitedMTRApollo Tyres 01/03 ### We partnered with SemiCab early because we trusted their vision for network-level logistics. Today, they are one of our top transport partners in India, combining strong service performance with a more sustainable, data-driven operating model. Sanchit Sasidhara Planning & Purchase, Asian Paints ### SemiCab has been a reliable partner for our first-mile vehicle placement requirements over the ### past six months. Their timely vehicle placements and cooperative team have supported the smooth functioning of our operations. We appreciate their responsiveness and service commitment, and look forward to continuing our association. MTR ### At Apollo Tyres, sustainability is a long-term commitment that extends across our entire value ### chain, including logistics. Our partnership with SemiCab has helped us rethink how our transportation network is planned and operated, bringing greater efficiency, reliability, and structural improvement into the system. We see SemiCab’s network-led approach as an important enabler in building a more responsible and future-ready supply chain. Rajshekhara Reddy Group head - Global Logistics, Apollo Tyres ## Frequently asked questions ### How is Orchestrated Collaboration™ different from contractual freight arrangements? Contracts coordinate predefined static commitments between a fixed set of parties. When demand, capacity or operating conditions change, the arrangement often becomes ineffective or may need to be renegotiated. Orchestrated Collaboration™ uses a neutral orchestration layer to continuously identify opportunities across the network dynamically, within each participant’s agreed commercial and operating constraints. ### How does network-wide optimization account for each participant’s priorities? Each participant’s service levels, commercial rules and operating constraints remain part of the plan. SemiCab activates opportunities where network-wide coordination creates additional value without requiring one participant to absorb another’s inefficiency. ### If procurement and TMS optimization are already in place, where does SemiCab find additional ### value? Procurement optimises the cost-service equation for a given lane or account, but it doesn't touch the empty-mile tax that every participant in the industry pays regardless.TMS optimises mode and partner selection one shipment at a time — it isn't built to see, let alone solve, network-wide inefficiency. SemiCab models the network that emerges dynamically across multiple TMS shipments at any given time, and creates value from what neither layer can reach: continuous moves, round trips, and better capacity positioning across the wider network. ### Does better performance for one participant come at the expense of another? No. The value comes from removing inefficiency from the network, rather than transferring margin between participants. Shippers gain lower and more predictable freight costs. LSPs and 3PLs gain differentiated network-level capabilities. Carriers gain more loaded miles and better asset utilization. ### How does SemiCab’s approach differ from load matching or brokerage? Load matching and brokerage primarily solve for individual shipments, often after demand appears. SemiCab plans across demand, capacity, locations and time horizons to create continuous moves, round trips, creating network-wide efficacies and reduced costs for all participants. ### Can freight optimization make a meaningful difference to emissions? Yes. Transportation accounts for approximately 25% of global energy-related CO₂ emissions, according to the International Energy Agency. SemiCab directly targets the biggest source of waste in a freight network: empty miles driven without moving goods. Elimination of empty miles also eliminates the CO2 emissions related to this waste. ## See what Apex finds in your network We'll work through your freight, your constraints and your objectives. Book a working session ## Footer [ ][4] Sign up for updates Email Address* **Thank you! ** You will soon hear from us... Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form. ### Socials [ LINKEDIN ][5] [ FACEBOOK ][6] [ YOUTUBE ][7] [ INSTAGRAM ][8] ### Email [ info@semicab.com ][9] ### Phone number [ +91-9187978070 ][10] SemiCab is a division of Algorhythm Holdings. [ Terms of Use ][11] © 2025 SemiCab Holdings, LLC [ Privacy Policy ][12][ Website Design Partner - Everything Design ][13] [1]: #main [2]: / [3]: / [4]: / [5]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/semicab [6]: https://www.facebook.com/semicab [7]: https://www.youtube.com/@SemiCab [8]: https://www.instagram.com/semicab_india/ [9]: mailto:info@semicab.com [10]: tel:+91-9187978070 [11]: /terms-of-use [12]: /privacy-policy [13]: https://www.everything.design/", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "Semicab — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Specializes in power management ICs and analog mixed-signal products, indicating design and manufacturing. | Semicab is an Indian semiconductor company specializing in power management ICs and analog mixed-signal products. | India | India", "role_description": "Solution Provider"}}, "X Score": "64", "Y Score": "62", "Overall Score": "63", "Industry Category": "ICT, Automation, Semiconductor / Semiconductors", "Quadrant": "Leaders"}, {"Company": "Silex Systems Limited", "Website": "https://www.silex.com.au", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "Australia", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(Australia)", "Operational Presence": "Australia", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Australian company developing SILEX laser enrichment technology for semiconductor-grade silicon and other materials.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Solution Provider", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "AU", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Silex Systems Limited — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Develops laser enrichment technology for semiconductor-grade silicon, contributing to semiconductor manufacturing.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Solution Provider", "verify_confidence": "90", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "silex.com.au", "data": {"company": {"name": "silex.com.au"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "OTCQX$-.--\nASX$NaN\n[[Logo/Rev]][1]\n* [About Us][2]\n  * [Values][3]\n  * [Leadership][4]\n  * [Corporate Governance][5]\n  * [ESG][6]\n* [Our Technology][7]\n  * [SILEX Laser Isotope Separation Technology][8]\n  * [SILEX Uranium Enrichment Technology][9]\n  * [Global Laser Enrichment][10]\n  * [SILEX Quantum Silicon Production for Quantum Computing][11]\n* [Investors][12]\n  * [ASX Announcements][13]\n  * [Financial Reports][14]\n  * [Presentations][15]\n  * [Research and Coverage][16]\n  * [Corporate Calendar][17]\n  * [Share Registry][18]\n  * [FAQs][19]\n* [News & Media][20]\n* [Contact Us][21]\n\n# Silex Systems Limited\n\nCommercialising our unique SILEX laser-based enrichment technology\n\n## Investor Presentation\n\nSilex Systems Limited (ASX: SLX) (OTCQX: SILXY) (“Silex”) is an Australian technology company\nfocused on the commercialisation of our innovative SILEX laser-based enrichment technology.\n\n[Download][22]\n\n## Our Technology\n\nWe’re proud to be an Australian technology company driving innovation on a global scale with the\ncommercialisation of our proprietary laser-based isotope separation technology.\n\n[\n\n### SILEX Laser Isotope Separation Technology\n\nThe SILEX Laser Isotope Separation (LIS) technology was invented by Silex Systems scientists Dr\nMichael…\n\nLearn more\n][23][\n\n### SILEX Uranium Enrichment Technology\n\nSilex invented and developed the ‘SILEX’ laser isotope separation technology in Sydney during the\n1990’s…\n\nLearn more\n][24][\n\n### Global Laser Enrichment (GLE)\n\nGLE is the exclusive licensee of the SILEX uranium enrichment technology. GLE is a\njointly-controlled venture…\n\nLearn more\n][25][\n\n### Quantum Silicon (Q-Si) Production for Quantum Computing\n\nSilex’s Q-Si Production Project, which commenced in August 2023, is being undertaken in conjunction\nwith…\n\nLearn more\n][26]\n\n### Silex Systems Limited\n\nSilex (ASX: SLX) (OTCQX: SILXY) is an Australian technology company focused on the commercialisation\nof our innovative SILEX laser-based enrichment technology for application to three key global\nmarkets:\n* [Uranium production and enrichment (nuclear power)][27]\n* [Silicon enrichment (silicon quantum computing)][28]\n* [Medical isotope enrichment (new cancer therapies)][29]\n\n[INVESTOR RELATIONS][30]\n\n### Our flagship Uranium Project:\n\nPaducah, Kentucky (US) Project – potentially a ‘Tier 1’ uranium resource\n* Opportunity for low-cost production of up to 5 million pounds uranium oxide annually for up to 30\n  years\n* Add-on opportunity to enrich further to produce low enriched uranium (LEU) and LEU+ for today’s\n  conventional nuclear reactor fleet\n* Additional opportunity to further enrich to high assay LEU (HALEU) for next generation advanced\n  reactors, including small modular reactors (SMRs)\n\n[Learn more][31]\n\n### Our Quantum Silicon Production Project:\n\nQuantum Silicon (Q-Si) Production for Quantum Computing\n* Opportunity to establish Silex as a key global supplier of enriched silicon\n* Enriched silicon is an enabling material for silicon quantum computing – leading technology for\n  the emerging quantum computing industry\n\n[Learn more][32]\n\n## Listed information\n\n### ASX:SLX\n\n### OTCQX:SILXY\n\nSubscribe to our announcements\nName\nEmail\nSubmit\n[[Logo/Rev]][33][enquiries@silex.com.au][34][investor.relations@silex.com.au][35][+61 2 9704\n8888][36]\n\nRegistered Office\n\nLucas Heights Science & Technology Centre, New Illawarra Road\nLucas Heights NSW 2234\nAustralia\n\nPostal Address\n\nPO Box 75\nMenai Central NSW 2234\nAustralia\n* [Home][37]\n* [About Us][38]\n* [Corporate][39]\n* [ESG][40]\n* [Our Technology][41]\n* [Our Investors][42]\n* [News & Media][43]\n* [Contact Us][44]\n* [Forward Looking Statements][45]\n* [Privacy Policy][46]\n* [Image Accreditations][47]\n©2026 Silex, All rights reserved\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /corporate-values/values/\n[3]: /corporate-values/values/\n[4]: /corporate-values/leadership/\n[5]: /corporate-values/corporate-governance/\n[6]: /corporate-values/our-esg-commitment/\n[7]: /silex-technology/silex-laser-isotope-separation-technology/\n[8]: /sil"}}, "page_text": "OTCQX$-.-- ASX$NaN [[Logo/Rev]][1] * [About Us][2] * [Values][3] * [Leadership][4] * [Corporate Governance][5] * [ESG][6] * [Our Technology][7] * [SILEX Laser Isotope Separation Technology][8] * [SILEX Uranium Enrichment Technology][9] * [Global Laser Enrichment][10] * [SILEX Quantum Silicon Production for Quantum Computing][11] * [Investors][12] * [ASX Announcements][13] * [Financial Reports][14] * [Presentations][15] * [Research and Coverage][16] * [Corporate Calendar][17] * [Share Registry][18] * [FAQs][19] * [News & Media][20] * [Contact Us][21] # Silex Systems Limited Commercialising our unique SILEX laser-based enrichment technology ## Investor Presentation Silex Systems Limited (ASX: SLX) (OTCQX: SILXY) (“Silex”) is an Australian technology company focused on the commercialisation of our innovative SILEX laser-based enrichment technology. [Download][22] ## Our Technology We’re proud to be an Australian technology company driving innovation on a global scale with the commercialisation of our proprietary laser-based isotope separation technology. [ ### SILEX Laser Isotope Separation Technology The SILEX Laser Isotope Separation (LIS) technology was invented by Silex Systems scientists Dr Michael… Learn more ][23][ ### SILEX Uranium Enrichment Technology Silex invented and developed the ‘SILEX’ laser isotope separation technology in Sydney during the 1990’s… Learn more ][24][ ### Global Laser Enrichment (GLE) GLE is the exclusive licensee of the SILEX uranium enrichment technology. GLE is a jointly-controlled venture… Learn more ][25][ ### Quantum Silicon (Q-Si) Production for Quantum Computing Silex’s Q-Si Production Project, which commenced in August 2023, is being undertaken in conjunction with… Learn more ][26] ### Silex Systems Limited Silex (ASX: SLX) (OTCQX: SILXY) is an Australian technology company focused on the commercialisation of our innovative SILEX laser-based enrichment technology for application to three key global markets: * [Uranium production and enrichment (nuclear power)][27] * [Silicon enrichment (silicon quantum computing)][28] * [Medical isotope enrichment (new cancer therapies)][29] [INVESTOR RELATIONS][30] ### Our flagship Uranium Project: Paducah, Kentucky (US) Project – potentially a ‘Tier 1’ uranium resource * Opportunity for low-cost production of up to 5 million pounds uranium oxide annually for up to 30 years * Add-on opportunity to enrich further to produce low enriched uranium (LEU) and LEU+ for today’s conventional nuclear reactor fleet * Additional opportunity to further enrich to high assay LEU (HALEU) for next generation advanced reactors, including small modular reactors (SMRs) [Learn more][31] ### Our Quantum Silicon Production Project: Quantum Silicon (Q-Si) Production for Quantum Computing * Opportunity to establish Silex as a key global supplier of enriched silicon * Enriched silicon is an enabling material for silicon quantum computing – leading technology for the emerging quantum computing industry [Learn more][32] ## Listed information ### ASX:SLX ### OTCQX:SILXY Subscribe to our announcements Name Email Submit [[Logo/Rev]][33][enquiries@silex.com.au][34][investor.relations@silex.com.au][35][+61 2 9704 8888][36] Registered Office Lucas Heights Science & Technology Centre, New Illawarra Road Lucas Heights NSW 2234 Australia Postal Address PO Box 75 Menai Central NSW 2234 Australia * [Home][37] * [About Us][38] * [Corporate][39] * [ESG][40] * [Our Technology][41] * [Our Investors][42] * [News & Media][43] * [Contact Us][44] * [Forward Looking Statements][45] * [Privacy Policy][46] * [Image Accreditations][47] ©2026 Silex, All rights reserved [1]: / [2]: /corporate-values/values/ [3]: /corporate-values/values/ [4]: /corporate-values/leadership/ [5]: /corporate-values/corporate-governance/ [6]: /corporate-values/our-esg-commitment/ [7]: /silex-technology/silex-laser-isotope-separation-technology/ [8]: /silex-technology/silex-laser-isotope-separation-technology/ [9]: /silex-technology/silex-uranium-enrichment-technology/ [10]: /silex-technology/global-laser-enrichment/ [11]: /silex-technology/silex-zs-si-production-for-quantum-computing/ [12]: /investors/announcements/ [13]: /investors/announcements/ [14]: /investors/reports/ [15]: /investors/presentations/ [16]: /investors/research-and-coverage/ [17]: /investors/corporate-calendar/ [18]: /investors/share-registry/ [19]: /investors/faqs/ [20]: /news-media/ [21]: /contact-us/ [22]: https://clients3.weblink.com.au/pdf/SLX/03060799.pdf [23]: /silex-technology/silex-laser-isotope-separation-technology/ [24]: /silex-technology/silex-uranium-enrichment-technology/ [25]: /silex-technology/global-laser-enrichment/ [26]: /silex-technology/silex-zs-si-production-for-quantum-computing/ [27]: /silex-technology/silex-uranium-enrichment-technology/ [28]: /silex-technology/silex-zs-si-production-for-quantum-computing/ [29]: /silex-technology/silex-laser-isotope-separation-technology/ [30]: /investors/announcements/ [31]: /silex-technology/silex-uranium-enrichment-technology/ [32]: /silex-technology/silex-zs-si-production-for-quantum-computing/ [33]: / [34]: mailto:enquiries@silex.com.au [35]: mailto:investor.relations@silex.com.au [36]: tel:+61 2 9704 8888 [37]: / [38]: / [39]: /corporate-values/corporate-governance/ [40]: /corporate-values/our-esg-commitment/ [41]: /silex-technology/silex-laser-isotope-separation-technology/ [42]: /investors/announcements/ [43]: /news-media/ [44]: /contact-us/ [45]: /forward-looking-statements/ [46]: /privacy-policy/ [47]: /image-accreditations/", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "Silex Systems Limited — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Develops laser enrichment technology for semiconductor-grade silicon, contributing to semiconductor manufacturing. | Australian company developing SILEX laser enrichment technology for semiconductor-grade silicon and other materials. | Australia | Australia", "role_description": "Solution Provider"}}, "X Score": "64", "Y Score": "62", "Overall Score": "63", "Industry Category": "ICT, Automation, Semiconductor / Semiconductors", "Quadrant": "Leaders"}, {"Company": "CDIL (Continental Device India)", "Website": "https://www.cdil.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "India", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(India)", "Operational Presence": "India", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "One of India's oldest semiconductor companies, manufacturing discrete devices and modules.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Solution Provider", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "CDIL (Continental Device India) — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Manufactures discrete devices and modules, builds/owns technology.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Solution Provider", "verify_confidence": "90", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "cdil.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "cdil.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "* [Home][1]\n* Devices\n  * [All Devices][2]\n  * [Diodes][3]\n  * [Transistors][4]\n  * [Power Transistors][5]\n  * [MOSFETs][6]\n  * [Rectifiers][7]\n  * [Triacs & SCRs][8]\n  * [TVS][9]\n  * [Regulators][10]\n  * [Solar Diode Modules][11]\n  * [Metal Can][12]\n* Sectors\n  * [Defence][13]\n  * [Automotive][14]\n* About Us\n  * [Company Profile][15]\n  * [Facilities and R&D][16]\n  * [Worldwide Reach][17]\n  * [Clients & Recognition][18]\n* [Contact][19]\n* [Careers][20]\n* [Home][21]\n* Devices\n  * [All Devices][22]\n  * [Diodes][23]\n  * [Transistors][24]\n  * [Power Transistors][25]\n  * [MOSFETs][26]\n  * [Rectifiers][27]\n  * [Triacs & SCRs][28]\n  * [TVS][29]\n  * [Regulators][30]\n  * [Solar Diode Modules][31]\n  * [Metal Can][32]\n* Sectors\n  * [Defence][33]\n  * [Automotive][34]\n* About Us\n  * [Company Profile][35]\n  * [Facilities and R&D][36]\n  * [Worldwide Reach][37]\n  * [Clients & Recognition][38]\n* [Contact][39]\n* [Careers][40]\n\n# [ [Continental Device India Ltd (CDIL)] Continental Device India Ltd (CDIL) ][41]\n\n## Continental Device India Ltd\n\n# Welcome to CDIL\n\nContinental Device India Pvt. Ltd., (CDIL) is a pioneer and a world class Semiconductor Manufacturer\nof silicon chips and devices since 1964.\n\nWith 60 years of semiconductor manufacturing experience, strict standards of quality, constant\nimprovements in R&D, technology, and processes, and the hard work of a team of dedicated\nprofessionals, CDIL today is an Indian brand that is recognized globally. \n\nAs India is poised for rapid take off and is set to become a manufacturing centre for the world, we\ntoo look forward to setting new standards of excellence in electronics and introducing our range of\nproducts and services to the furthest corners of the globe. \n\n# News & Updates\n\nNews\n[\n][42]\nFebruary 13, 2025\n[ Make in India Milestone – CDIL Launches India’s First High-Efficiency Semiconductors for Solar\nApplications ][43]\nFebruary 13, 2025\n\nCDIL Semiconductors unveiled the nation’s first indigenous **Solar Bypass Diodes**, a breakthrough\nthat significantly enhances solar panel efficiency and longevity. This innovation represents a leap\nforward in India’s renewable energy ambitions.\n\n[Read more →][44]\nFebruary 13, 2025\n[\n][45]\nFebruary 1, 2025\n[ Meet Team CDIL at Source India 2025, Chennai! ][46]\nFebruary 1, 2025\n\n**CDIL Semiconductors** will be participating in the **14th Source India – Electronics Supply\nChain** event, organized by **ELCINA** on **February 18-19, 2025**, at the **Chennai Trade Centre**.\n\n[Read more →][47]\nFebruary 1, 2025\n[\n][48]\nSeptember 28, 2023\n[ CDIL Semiconductors becomes the first Indian company to start production of Silicon Carbide\ndevices; aims to address the impending surge in Electric Vehicles, Power Management Devices and\nSolar Panels ][49]\nSeptember 28, 2023\n\nHon’ble Union Minister of State for Electronics and Information Technology, Shri Rajeev\nChandrasekhar, virtually inaugurated the new Surface Mount Semiconductor Packaging Line, at CDIL\nMohali plant today. With the new versatile SMA and SMB package line, via the GOI’s SPECS, CDIL\nbecomes India’s first Silicon Carbide components manufacturer.\n\n[Read more →][50]\nSeptember 28, 2023\n\n# Search for a Device\n\n**By Series or Device Number:**\nIN58XX, CMBZ52XX, BD139, CJD136 etc. \n\n**By Package Name/ Type:**\nTO3, DO214AB, KBPC, Metal Can, Plastic, SMD, Axial etc.\n\n**By Category/ Sub-Category:**\nZener, Medium Power, Schottky, DIAC etc.\n\nNo results found\n\nIf you are unable to find what you are looking for, browse components through the [device\npage][51] or send us an [email][52].\n\n# Featured Devices\n\nSolar Diode Modules\n[\n][53]\n[ CD40T45T ][54]\n$0.00\n\nModule 09-E Plastic Package\n\n40A Schottky Barrier Rectifier - Trench Type\n\n**Application **\n\nSolar Bypass and Forward applications\n\n***Device Types ***\n\nCD40T45T : Reverse Voltage - 45 Volts, Forward Current - 40 Ampere\n\n*See the data sheet for *[***CD40T45T***][55]\n\n[Read more →][56]\n[\n][57]\n[ CD50T45TD ][58]\n$0.00\n\nModule 09-E Plastic Package\n\n50A Schottky Barrier Recti"}}, "page_text": "* [Home][1] * Devices * [All Devices][2] * [Diodes][3] * [Transistors][4] * [Power Transistors][5] * [MOSFETs][6] * [Rectifiers][7] * [Triacs & SCRs][8] * [TVS][9] * [Regulators][10] * [Solar Diode Modules][11] * [Metal Can][12] * Sectors * [Defence][13] * [Automotive][14] * About Us * [Company Profile][15] * [Facilities and R&D][16] * [Worldwide Reach][17] * [Clients & Recognition][18] * [Contact][19] * [Careers][20] * [Home][21] * Devices * [All Devices][22] * [Diodes][23] * [Transistors][24] * [Power Transistors][25] * [MOSFETs][26] * [Rectifiers][27] * [Triacs & SCRs][28] * [TVS][29] * [Regulators][30] * [Solar Diode Modules][31] * [Metal Can][32] * Sectors * [Defence][33] * [Automotive][34] * About Us * [Company Profile][35] * [Facilities and R&D][36] * [Worldwide Reach][37] * [Clients & Recognition][38] * [Contact][39] * [Careers][40] # [ [Continental Device India Ltd (CDIL)] Continental Device India Ltd (CDIL) ][41] ## Continental Device India Ltd # Welcome to CDIL Continental Device India Pvt. Ltd., (CDIL) is a pioneer and a world class Semiconductor Manufacturer of silicon chips and devices since 1964. With 60 years of semiconductor manufacturing experience, strict standards of quality, constant improvements in R&D, technology, and processes, and the hard work of a team of dedicated professionals, CDIL today is an Indian brand that is recognized globally. As India is poised for rapid take off and is set to become a manufacturing centre for the world, we too look forward to setting new standards of excellence in electronics and introducing our range of products and services to the furthest corners of the globe. # News & Updates News [ ][42] February 13, 2025 [ Make in India Milestone – CDIL Launches India’s First High-Efficiency Semiconductors for Solar Applications ][43] February 13, 2025 CDIL Semiconductors unveiled the nation’s first indigenous **Solar Bypass Diodes**, a breakthrough that significantly enhances solar panel efficiency and longevity. This innovation represents a leap forward in India’s renewable energy ambitions. [Read more →][44] February 13, 2025 [ ][45] February 1, 2025 [ Meet Team CDIL at Source India 2025, Chennai! ][46] February 1, 2025 **CDIL Semiconductors** will be participating in the **14th Source India – Electronics Supply Chain** event, organized by **ELCINA** on **February 18-19, 2025**, at the **Chennai Trade Centre**. [Read more →][47] February 1, 2025 [ ][48] September 28, 2023 [ CDIL Semiconductors becomes the first Indian company to start production of Silicon Carbide devices; aims to address the impending surge in Electric Vehicles, Power Management Devices and Solar Panels ][49] September 28, 2023 Hon’ble Union Minister of State for Electronics and Information Technology, Shri Rajeev Chandrasekhar, virtually inaugurated the new Surface Mount Semiconductor Packaging Line, at CDIL Mohali plant today. With the new versatile SMA and SMB package line, via the GOI’s SPECS, CDIL becomes India’s first Silicon Carbide components manufacturer. [Read more →][50] September 28, 2023 # Search for a Device **By Series or Device Number:** IN58XX, CMBZ52XX, BD139, CJD136 etc. **By Package Name/ Type:** TO3, DO214AB, KBPC, Metal Can, Plastic, SMD, Axial etc. **By Category/ Sub-Category:** Zener, Medium Power, Schottky, DIAC etc. No results found If you are unable to find what you are looking for, browse components through the [device page][51] or send us an [email][52]. # Featured Devices Solar Diode Modules [ ][53] [ CD40T45T ][54] $0.00 Module 09-E Plastic Package 40A Schottky Barrier Rectifier - Trench Type **Application ** Solar Bypass and Forward applications ***Device Types *** CD40T45T : Reverse Voltage - 45 Volts, Forward Current - 40 Ampere *See the data sheet for *[***CD40T45T***][55] [Read more →][56] [ ][57] [ CD50T45TD ][58] $0.00 Module 09-E Plastic Package 50A Schottky Barrier Rectifier - Dual Trench Type **Application ** Solar Bypass and Forward applications ***Device Types *** CD50T45TD : Reverse Voltage - 45 Volts, Forward Current - 50 Ampere *See the data sheet for *[***CD50T45TD***][59] [Read more →][60] ## [Company Information][61] [ [CDIL HQ | CDIL Semiconductors.png] ][62] Spread between Delhi and Mohali, CDIL's four semiconductor manufacturing units have total process control, right from the design and development stage, earning them ISO 9001, IATF 16949, ISO 14001 and OHSAS 18001 certifications. ## [Products & DEVICES][63] [ [Home-Devices | CDIL Semiconductors.png] ][64] A comprehensive range of semiconductor chips and devices include Diffused Wafers, Transistors, Diodes, Rectifiers, Thyristors, TVSs and Regulators with specialities in Metal Can and custom designed packages. ## Worldwide Reach [ [World-Map-Orange.png] ][65] A deep sales and distribution network, both locally and globally, reaches satisfied customers in over 35 countries across 45 locations. An international office in Hong Kong manages international clients. # Group Companies & Divisions [ [Deltron, an ISO 9001:2000 and TS 16949 company, is one of India’s leading contract manufacturers of Electronic assemblies. Deltron counts some of the most respected original equipment manufacturers in the world as its customers.] ][66] Deltron, an ISO9001:2015 and IATF 16949 company, is one of India’s leading contract manufacturers of Electronic assemblies. Deltron counts some of the most respected original equipment manufacturers in the world as its customers. ### Head Office C-120 Naraina Industrial Area -I New Delhi - 110028 (+91) 11 4141 1112 (+91) 11 2579 6150 email@cdil.com ### Connect [Careers][67] [Warranty Terms][68] [Privacy Policy][69] [Notices][70] ### Division Sites [Deltron][71] ### Assurance of Quality An ISO 9001, IATF 16949, ISO/IEC 27001, ISO 14001, ISO 45001 & Zed Certified Company Copyright 2026, Continental Device India Pvt. Ltd. All rights reserved. [1]: / [2]: /devices-1 [3]: /diodes [4]: /transistors [5]: /power-transistors [6]: /mosfets [7]: /rectifiers [8]: /triacs [9]: /tvs [10]: /regulators [11]: /solar-diode-modules [12]: /metal-can-transistors [13]: /defence [14]: /automotive [15]: /company-profile [16]: /research-development [17]: /worldwide-reach [18]: /recognition [19]: /contact [20]: /careers [21]: / [22]: /devices-1 [23]: /diodes [24]: /transistors [25]: /power-transistors [26]: /mosfets [27]: /rectifiers [28]: /triacs [29]: /tvs [30]: /regulators [31]: /solar-diode-modules [32]: /metal-can-transistors [33]: /defence [34]: /automotive [35]: /company-profile [36]: /research-development [37]: /worldwide-reach [38]: /recognition [39]: /contact [40]: /careers [41]: / [42]: /news/2025/2/22/make-in-india-milestone-cdil-launches-indias-first-high-efficiency-semiconduct ors-for-solar-applications [43]: /news/2025/2/22/make-in-india-milestone-cdil-launches-indias-first-high-efficiency-semiconduct ors-for-solar-applications [44]: /news/2025/2/22/make-in-india-milestone-cdil-launches-indias-first-high-efficiency-semiconduct ors-for-solar-applications [45]: /news/2025/2/22/meet-team-cdil-at-source-india-2025-chennai [46]: /news/2025/2/22/meet-team-cdil-at-source-india-2025-chennai [47]: /news/2025/2/22/meet-team-cdil-at-source-india-2025-chennai [48]: /n