][65] [ NetQ Real-time AI data center network observability ][66] [ UFM InfiniBand data center fabric management platform ][67] [ Pure SONiC Open-source Linux network OS for switches ][68] Support [ Enterprise Support Portal NVIDIA Enterprise Application Hub login portal ][69] [ Firmware Download NVIDIA Networking firmware download center ][70] [ End-of-life Products End-of-life and support status for products ][71] [ Product Documentation NVIDIA networking product and software documentation ][72] [ InfiniBand Drivers InfiniBand and VPI software downloads and drivers ][73] [ Ethernet Drivers Ethernet adapter drivers and acceleration software ][74] [Buy][75] This site requires Javascript in order to view all its content. Please enable Javascript in order to access all the functionality of this web site. Here are the [instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser.][76] # The Network Defines the AI Data Center Next-generation networking for high-performance, scalable, and secure gigascale AI factories. * [Introduction][77] * [Technology][78] * [Benefits][79] * [News][80] * [Resources][81] * [Introduction][82] * [Technology][83] * [Benefits][84] * [News][85] * [Resources][86] * [Introduction][87] * [Technology][88] * [Benefits][89] * [News][90] * [Resources][91] [ Contact Us ][92] Introduction ## Networking Purpose-Built for the Era of AI Factories [AI factories][93] now span tens of thousands of GPUs—and soon, millions—operating as a single distributed computing engine. To keep accelerators fully utilized, AI workloads demand deterministic latency, lossless throughput, stable iteration times, and the ability to scale not only within a data center, but across multiple sites. NVIDIA networking delivers the full-stack fabric that makes this possible, combining [NVIDIA NVLink™][94] scale-up, [NVIDIA Quantum InfiniBand][95] and [Spectrum-X™ Ethernet][96] scale-out, Spectrum-XGS multi-data-center scale-across, [NVIDIA® BlueField® DPU][97] and [DOCA™][98] for infrastructure services, and next-generation [silicon-photonics platforms][99] to power the world’s most advanced AI factories. ## Inside the NVIDIA Rubin Platform: Six New Chips, One AI Supercomputer Learn how Spectrum-6, BlueField-4, and ConnectX®-9 make up the extreme codesign foundation of the Rubin platform. [Read the Blog ][100] ## NVIDIA Vera Rubin POD: One AI Supercomputer, Five Rack-Scale Systems Learn how a unified MGX architecture allows operators to quickly scale custom AI factories for agentic apps using flexible, interchangeable interconnects. [Read the Blog ][101] [YouTube Video] Consent for Optional Cookies (googleCookiePolicyLink)YouTube sets performance, advertising, and other optional cookies(/googleCookiePolicyLink) when you watch embedded videos. To watch this video, you need to turn on optional cookies for the site. By clicking “Accept and Play Video,” you will automatically turn on advertising and other optional cookies for the site and accept our (nvidiaTermsOfServiceLink)Terms of Service(/nvidiaTermsOfServiceLink) (which contains important waivers). Please see our (nvidiaPrivacyPolicyLink)Privacy Policy(/nvidiaPrivacyPolicyLink) and (nvidiaCookiePolicyLink)Cookie Policy(/nvidiaCookiePolicyLink) for more information. Cancel Accept and Play Video Alternatively, you can (youtubeLink)watch this video on YouTube(/youtubeLink). [AI factory operating system powered by NVIDIA BlueField-4 DPUs] ## NVIDIA Launches BlueField-4: The Processor Powering the Operating System of AI Factories [ Learn More ][102] [ An image of a switch chip with many silicon photonics modules co-located on the same chip package. ] ## New Co-Packaged Silicon Photonic Networking Switches to Scale to Millions of GPUs, Multi-Site AI ## Factories [ Learn More ][103] ### Technology ## The Innovations Defining NVIDIA AI Networking NVIDIA builds networking as part of an integrated AI platform—combining GPUs, SuperNIC™s, DPUs, switches, optics, and software into an extreme codesigned architecture that delivers uncompromised, predictable performance at scale. [NVIDIA Spectrum-X Networking Platform] ##### Accelerated Ethernet Networking for AI The NVIDIA Spectrum-X Ethernet platform is purpose-built for AI, delivering 1.6x higher network performance than off-the-shelf (OTS) Ethernet. Spectrum-XGS Ethernet scale-across technology enables high-performance AI fabrics that span racks, buildings, and entire campuses. [Learn About Ethernet Solutions ][104] [Learn About NVIDIA Spectrum-X Ethernet ][105] [Learn About Data Center Simulation ][106] [NVIDIA Quantum-X800 Platform] ##### InfiniBand for AI and Scientific Computing With ultra-low latency, in-network computing, and next-generation silicon-photonics CPO systems, the NVIDIA Quantum InfiniBand architecture provides the industry’s fastest, most scalable networking for AI and HPC. [Learn About InfiniBand Solutions ][107] [Learn About NVIDIA Quantum-X800 ][108] [Learn About Silicon Photonics ][109] [NVIDIA BlueField Networking Platform] ##### Accelerated Computing for Data Center Infrastructure The NVIDIA BlueField platform combines high-speed networking with powerful computing to accelerate data center infrastructure, unlocking new levels of performance, efficiency, and security for the world’s AI data centers. [Learn About NVIDIA BlueField DPUs ][110] [Learn About NVIDIA DOCA ][111] ### Benefits ## Accelerated Networking for AI Factories [Performance] ### Accelerated Performance NVIDIA networking delivers a full-stack, accelerator-optimized fabric that minimizes tail latency, stabilizes iteration times, and keeps GPUs fully utilized across training and inference. [Gigascale AI] ### Gigascale NVIDIA networking enables gigascale growth with high-radix switching, co-packaged optics, and Spectrum-XGS Ethernet technology that unify facilities into one high-performance AI fabric. [Security] ### Security and Visibility Data visualization and isolation are essential security functionalities for every data center, and NVIDIA networking solutions enhance security, simplify data center automation, and provide complete visibility into your network. [Orchestration] ### Orchestration Scalable, modern network operations frameworks such as NetQ, UFM, and DOCA use network telemetry to deliver AI-powered cyber intelligence and analytics to ensure your AI network fabric operates smoothly. [Simulation] ### Simulation Build digital twins of data center networks with NVIDIA DSX Air—a cloud-hosted virtual environment for design, testing, and validation of network provisioning, autom", "discovery_snippets": [], "classify": {"summary": "Mellanox Technologies — channel participant (openai_web_search_discover). Verify: Develops networking semiconductors; acquired by Nvidia. | Develops semiconductors for networking; acquired by Nvidia. | Israel | Israel", "role_description": "Solution Provider"}}, "X Score": "55", "Y Score": "54", "Overall Score": "54", "Industry Category": "ICT, Automation, Semiconductor / Semiconductors", "Quadrant": "Challengers"}, {"Company": "Western Digital", "Website": "https://www.westerndigital.com", "Founded": "Not publicly disclosed", "Headquarters": "USA", "Continent / Geography": "NA(United States)", "Operational Presence": "United States", "Ownership": "Not publicly disclosed", "Employees": "Not publicly disclosed", "Core Categories": "Not publicly disclosed", "Specialty Focus": "Manufactures NAND flash and HDDs.", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Solution Provider", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "US", "Region Code": "NA", "Summary": "Western Digital — channel participant (chatgpt_recall). Verify: Western Digital manufactures NAND flash and HDDs, which are semiconductor-based products.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "Data Confidence": "Medium", "Quality Score": "3", "commercial_role": "Solution Provider", "verify_confide